+# Intake and review corrections for Vloer dogfooding
+
+Date: 2026-09-09. Source baseline: `67c4bc968455a99ef767bc8a24791ea1a87319cb`. Status: source-reviewed candidate; not deployed, compiled or execution-qualified in the preparation environment.
+
+These corrections address three findings from the Ploeg/De Vloer product audit. `PV-013`, `PV-015` and `PV-074` are design-plan identifiers, not native tracker IDs or authorization to dispatch work. No tracker mutation, forge publication or release was performed while preparing the changes.
+
+## Authoritative tracker Scope: PV-013
+
+`Server.mirror` fetched the provider's current Work Item, then unconditionally replaced its `ExternalScope` with `TrackerEvent.Scope.ID`. ClickUp assignment events can omit the List while the authoritative fetch includes it. The replacement erased the routing key before `pinTeam` and `resolveTarget`. A conflicting nonempty event Scope could also override the fetched identity.
+
+The candidate preserves a nonempty fetched Scope, falls back to the event Scope when the provider's read does not supply one, and rejects a conflicting pair with HTTP 409 before routing or ingestion. Structured warning fields include the provider, item ID and both scopes. Fetch-failure and webhook-snapshot fallback behavior is preserved; this is not the stronger fail-closed admission contract planned for a future WorkOrder.
+
+`pkg/httpapi/mirror_test.go` exercises signed ClickUp payload parsing, an authenticated task fetch against `httptest`, team and target resolution, conflict rejection before database access, matching scopes and legacy fallbacks. These tests were source-reviewed but not executed here.
+
+Remaining scope: durable rejection audit, connection-scoped external identity, stricter unresolved-target handling and reconciliation of material tracker changes. The existing target model is retained; proposed ADR 0015 is not represented as fully implemented. The OpenSpec change is `preserve-authoritative-tracker-scope`.
+
+## Authenticated forge deduplication: PV-015
+
+`handleForgeWebhook` called `SeenDelivery` before `ParseWebhook`. A request with a forged signature could therefore occupy a real delivery ID and cause its later authentic delivery to be discarded. The candidate authenticates and parses the bounded original bytes before any deduplication or forge audit operation. Even a known delivery ID is authenticated again.
+
+The existing one-MiB provider body limit is enforced explicitly at the receiver. Declared or streamed overflow is rejected with 413; body-read failure is rejected with 400. Signature bytes are preserved, including whitespace and UTF-8. Existing HTTP Content-Type compatibility and provider algorithms are retained. The provider still parses JSON; no new media-type policy is claimed.
+
+`pkg/httpapi/forge_admission_test.go` contains invalid-then-valid same-ID regressions for invalid/missing/short signatures, authenticated malformed JSON, body-read failure and both overflow modes. It also covers an altered body using a known ID and a valid payload exactly at the limit. No execution or red-against-original result is claimed.
+
+This restores the existing verify→deduplicate→audit intent in `openspec/changes/close-the-review-loop/`; it introduces no new architectural authority. The separate delivery-ID and audit transactions still have a crash-loss window. A transactional inbox/outbox and a versioned HTTP admission policy remain future work. The source fix must not be described as exactly-once processing.
+
+## Explicit review approval: PV-074
+
+When fix-round evaluation reached the verdict step, absence of `request_changes` returned `review_approved`. That included a missing verdict and failed reviewer. The candidate requires successful, exact `approve` outcomes from every configured final reading Role. Missing, malformed, inconclusive, failed, conflicting, wrong-round or writer-only evidence cannot confer approval.
+
+An incomplete review closes the Shift with `review_incomplete`, leaves the Work Item `needs_human`, preserves original reports and creates no new paid work. The existing pool-before-cap-before-verdict order and bounded request-changes pairs remain intact. Disabled fix loops still stop with `plan_exhausted`; exhausted budgets or caps retain their own reasons. No historical approvals are rewritten.
+
+Tracker handoff wording reports that a pull request was opened and requires checks and approvals before merge. It no longer claims that the existence of a PR means the item is finished. Existing tracker completion behavior remains unchanged: Ploeg does not mark the task delivered to production.
+
+The strengthened `TestLoop_NoVerdictEndsThePlan` and new `reviewapproval_test.go` cover 18 decision cases, failed-reader expiry and re-evaluation, immutable evidence, retained spend through a fix pair, human handoff and writer-only denial. Independent source review found no concrete type/logic defect; that is not a Go compiler or database result. The OpenSpec change is `require-explicit-review-approval`.
+
+## Verification and acceptance boundary
+
+`git diff --check` passed. Go and gofmt are absent. The official Go 1.25.0 download was attempted once; the environment returned `network approval was cancelled before a decision was returned`. No alternative download route was attempted. Helm and Docker are also absent.
+
+The repository's Go tests use embedded PostgreSQL in `TestMain`. They require a non-root execution user and the binary/dependency cache or an authorized contributor/CI network. Merely running a pure test name within those packages still invokes TestMain. Do not count a skipped or unavailable database as a passing test.
+
+Required before acceptance:
+
+```sh
+gofmt -l .
+go vet ./...
+go build ./...
+go test ./pkg/httpapi/ ./pkg/shiftengine/
+go test ./...
+helm lint ops/helm/ploeg
+helm template ploeg ops/helm/ploeg
+helm template ploeg ops/helm/ploeg -f ops/helm/ploeg/ci/executor-values.yaml
+helm template ploeg ops/helm/ploeg -f ops/helm/ploeg/ci/executor-cronjob-values.yaml
+helm template ploeg ops/helm/ploeg -f ops/helm/ploeg/ci/executor-gitlab-values.yaml
+./scripts/helm-golden.sh check
+./scripts/brand-marks.sh
+```
+
+The formatting gate must report no files; apply gofmt if it reports any. Run the regressions against the old behavior in an isolated checkout, preserving both failing and corrected results. `TestLoop_NoVerdictEndsThePlan` provides a directly executable old-source comparison. The mirror signature changed, so a pre-fix comparison must adapt the old call signature or restore the old overwrite behavior inside the candidate signature; a compilation failure alone is not proof of the regression. For the forge case, restore only the old dedup-before-parse order while retaining the test helpers, and assert that a rejected request reserved the ID.
+
+This batch does not qualify Ploeg for shared unattended execution. Worker management-key isolation, authenticated worker control, conservative crash accounting, trusted candidate verification and fenced publication remain separate prerequisites in the product audit.
