+---
+status: proposed
+date: 2026-09-09
+---
+
+# Preserve authoritative tracker scope
+
+## Why
+
+The ClickUp Tracker Provider reads a task's native List into `WorkItem.ExternalScope`, but `Server.mirror` overwrites it with the empty Scope from a thin webhook. `pinTeam` and `resolveTarget` consequently cannot select the configured Team and Work Target. A nonempty stale webhook Scope can also replace a different current Scope returned by the Tracker Provider.
+
+This is the tracker ingest seam, supporting Ploeg backlog #31 and the De Vloer product backlog PV-013. The current Tracker Provider contract already says that the provider read is authoritative and that webhook content is a fallback.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Preserve a nonempty Scope from the authoritative read.
+- Use the normalized event Scope when a successful read supplies no Scope, preserving the current Vikunja compatibility path.
+- Reject different nonempty event and fetched Scopes before Team pinning, Work Target resolution or Work Item ingestion; return HTTP 409 with structured diagnostic evidence.
+- Retain the existing webhook snapshot and event-only fallbacks when the read fails.
+- Add signed ClickUp parse/fetch/routing and conflict rejection regression coverage.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `tracker-scope-integrity`: reconcile native tracker Scope evidence before routing a Work Item.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None of the existing published OpenSpec capabilities changes.
+
+## Impact
+
+`pkg/httpapi/server.go` and `pkg/httpapi/mirror_test.go`. The internal `mirror` method gains an error result; the Tracker Provider SPI, Run API and stored schema stay compatible. HTTP 409 is a new tracker webhook rejection response.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+This change does not add connection identity, strict rejection of every unmapped target, a transactional tracker inbox, a durable rejection audit row, task move reconciliation, unassignment handling, a new queue, or tracker/forge write-backs. It does not change claim predicates, KEDA scaling queries, Lease ownership or budgets. The tracker remains the source of Work Item content, consistent with `docs/design.md` §2.
