+# Correct the existing review handoff
+
+## Context
+
+`nextFixRound` currently returns `review_approved` for any reports without a
+request for changes. `RoundReports` includes expired readers, and a reading
+Run may omit its verdict. `close` already parks configured Shifts at
+`needs_human`; `notifyTracker` already leaves tracker tasks open. The defect is
+false approval evidence and completion wording, not an automatic merge path.
+
+Architecture section 9.18 describes one earlier cause of missing verdicts,
+but the current drop-box support does not make every verdict present. This
+change is based on the current engine and store code, not that historical gap.
+
+## Implementation
+
+Keep the existing pool, cap and verdict evaluation order described by
+[ADR-0017](../../../docs/adrs/0017-the-review-loop-is-verdict-driven-and-capped.md).
+Preserve its distinction between closing a Shift and requesting another fix
+Round. Closure without a verdict remains a human handoff; it no longer claims
+approval. ADR-0017 is proposed and is not ratified by this correction.
+
+Compare current-round reports against the final configured Round's reading
+Roles. Require every Role to be represented by successful explicit approval;
+reject inconclusive evidence, including conflicting duplicate reports. A
+writer or an earlier Round cannot satisfy the set. A current reader requesting
+changes retains precedence and the same bounded writer/reviewer pair.
+
+`review_incomplete` carries an explicit human-review explanation through the
+existing close path. Tracker prose states that a pull request was opened and
+that required checks and approvals must pass before merge. No stored verdict,
+OutcomeReport type, outcome enum or schema changes.
+
+## Compatibility and crash behavior
+
+ADR-0010's roster, ADR-0011's report transport, ADR-0012's budget pool and
+ADR-0013's reader/writer separation are unchanged. No claim predicate changes;
+the KEDA query stays unchanged. R2 recovery reads persisted evidence and reaches
+the same decision after restart. No historical shift or report is backfilled.
+
+Human handoff remains terminal for the current Shift and `needs_human` for the
+Work Item, with no new paid attempt. Forge-triggered Follow-Ups are separate
+work. Required reviewers currently mean all configured reading Roles in the
+final Round; optional-reviewer/quorum policies require a later explicit design.
+
+## Validation
+
+Table-driven engine tests cover required-role omissions, failed and unknown
+Outcomes, malformed verdicts, earlier-round and writer approvals, complete
+approval and request-changes precedence. Lifecycle tests expire a real reader,
+verify the human handoff and unchanged evidence, and exercise the next fix
+pair. Existing budget and cap tests remain gates. The no-verdict lifecycle
+regression must fail against the original engine before the fix is accepted.
