@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Require explicit review approval
+
+## Why
+
+PV-074 in the Ploeg/Vloer product backlog identifies a false approval in
+`pkg/shiftengine/reviewloop.go`: absence of `request_changes` currently produces
+`review_approved`. A missing report, unsuccessful reading Run or omitted verdict
+can therefore appear approved. R2 and R3 require a failed Run to remain visible.
+
+## What changes
+
+The Shift advancement seam will require a successful explicit approval from
+every configured reading Role in the final review Round. With no request for
+changes and incomplete approval evidence, the existing human handoff will carry
+`review_incomplete`. Tracker wording will describe the pull request accurately
+without claiming that the Work Item is finished.
+
+The existing bounded request-changes loop, historical reports and human merge
+authority remain unchanged. This corrects the meaning of the existing verdict
+contract; it does not create a new Run API or dispatch policy.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+No Follow-Up ingestion, reviewer retries, automatic merge, new reviewer quorum
+configuration, budget reset, candidate revision protocol or schema migration.
+The tracker remains authoritative under `docs/design.md` section 2.
+
+## Impact
+
+`pkg/shiftengine` and regression tests; existing `outcomereport.v1` remains the
+contract. `shifts.close_reason` is unconstrained text, so the additional reason
+does not change a published enum or require a migration.
